thelial cell intercalation before gastrulation.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>449</volume><fpage>1049</fpage><lpage>1052</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17928866</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Gilland1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilland</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Burke</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Gastrulation in Reptiles.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Stern</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-group><source>Gastrulation: from cells to embryo</source><publisher-loc>Cold Spring Harbor, NY</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Cold Spring Harbor Press</publisher-name><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>217</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Yntema1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yntema</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1968</year><article-title>A series of stages in the embryonic development of Chelydra serpentina.</article-title><source>J. Morphol.</source><volume>125</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>251</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5681661</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Guyot1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guyot</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Pieau</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Renous</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>D&#x000e9;veloppement embryonnaire d'une tortue terrestre, la tortue d'Hermann, <italic>Testudo hermanni</italic> Gmelin, 1789.</article-title><source>Annales des Sciences Naturelles, Zoologie, Paris</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>137</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-SaukaSpengler1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sauka-Spengler</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Baratte</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lepage</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Characterization of Brachyury genes in the dogfish S. canicula and the lamprey L. fluviatilis. Insights into gastrulation in a chondrichthyan.</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><volume>263</volume><fpage>296</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14597203</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Coolen1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coolen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sauka-Spengler</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicolle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Le-Mentec</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lallemand</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Evolution of axis specification mechanisms in jawed vertebrates: insights from a chondrichthyan.</article-title><source>PLoS ONE</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>e374</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17440610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Plouhinec1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Plouhinec</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Sauka-Spengler</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Germot</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Le Mentec</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cabana</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The mammalian Crx genes are highly divergent representatives of the Otx5 gene family, a gnathostome orthology class of orthodenticle-related homeogenes involved in the differentiation of retinal photoreceptors and circadian entrainment.</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>513</fpage><lpage>521</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12654938</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Dorizzi1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dorizzi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Richard-Mercier</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Pieau</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>The ovary retains male potential after the thermosensitive period for sex determination in the turtle Emys orbicularis.</article-title><source>Differentiation</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8765049</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-ChandrasekharanNayar1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chandrasekharan Nayar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1966</year><article-title>In vitro vital staining of chelonian blastoderms.</article-title><source>Indian JExpBio</source><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>134</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Pasteels1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pasteels</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1937</year><article-title>Etude sur la gastrulation des vert&#x000e9;br&#x000e9;s m&#x000e9;roblastiques. II. Reptiles.</article-title><source>Arch Biol</source><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>184</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002676-Holland1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="j